<title>JAPAN: M'bishi Heavy, others win $2 bln Saudi plant order.</title>
<headline>M'bishi Heavy, others win $2 bln Saudi plant order.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd said on Monday that it, Toyo Engineering Corp and ABB Lummus Global Inc of the United States have won a $2 billion order to build a petrochemical plant in Saudi Arabia.</p>
<p>The construction of the plant, ordered by a joint venture of the state-run Saudi Basic Industries Corp and Mobil Corp, is expected to be completed in 2000. The venture will be called Saudi Yanbu Petrochemical Corp.</p>
<p>The plant is expected to have the capacity to make 800,000 tonnes of ethylene, 410,000 tonnes of ethylene glycol, 535,000 tonnes of polyethylene and 260,000 tonnes of polypropylene annually.</p>
<p>The products will be exported to Asia and Europe.</p>
</text>
